# Build-time SEO defaults. Vite substitutes these into `index.html` wherever it
# finds `%VITE_…%`, so they are present in the raw HTML response — what a
# crawler reads before a single line of JavaScript has run. That matters here:
# the page is client-rendered, so without these there is nothing in the document
# for a search engine to summarise and it invents a snippet from whatever the
# rendered DOM happens to contain.
#
# Committed on purpose. These are public marketing copy, not secrets, and the
# deploy builds straight from the checkout — a value that only lived on one
# machine would silently vanish from production.
#
# The title and description can be overridden at runtime from the admin profile
# editor (stored in `site_settings`, served by `GET /api/home`, applied by
# `home.ts`). Leaving those blank keeps what is set here.

VITE_SITE_URL=https://www.andrewmccall.uk
VITE_SITE_TITLE=Andrew McCall - Newcastle-Upon-Tyne - Software Engineer
VITE_SITE_DESCRIPTION=A Nerdy North East Software Developer.
VITE_SITE_IMAGE=https://www.andrewmccall.uk/nojs.png
